From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:46:33 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-pico8

PICO-8 gets one shelf, Games/PICO8, on FAKE-08 (fake08) alone.
Platform::Pico8 is appended to SHELVES and Core::Fake08 to EVERY;
upstream's ALL lists stay as they are. Carts are .p8 (text, or a PNG cart
under that name) and <name>.p8.png; a bare .png never lands on the shelf.
A text cart is titled by its first comment line, a PNG cart by its file
name without .p8, _ read as a space. It plays like the NES: d-pad, O on B,
X on A, Start opens the cart's pause menu, slot owns L and R, X is turbo X
and Y turbo O. fake-08 offers no state, so rewind is off and the in-game
States page is hidden; cartdata keeps a cart's saves. The 128x128 picture
sits centred on a 240x160 canvas, so Actual (the default) draws it at
exactly 3x, 384x384, and Stretch fills the panel. Its own Screen section
holds Shader (Off and the retro list, Config/pico8_shader.txt) and
Picture (pico8 in picture.txt). The core gets Saves/PICO8 as its save
dir, so cartdata lands in Saves/PICO8/cdata. Released 2015-04-18 for the
shelf order. The shelf shows the Virtual Boy cart until the PICO-8 cart
lands.
